The first storyboard to draw is Tidy my calendar (published/an-edited-meeting-does-not-come-back.json; page https://riskmandate.ai/stories/an-edited-meeting-does-not-come-back.html). Its punchline is the one the site would most like on a wall: Delete is recoverable. Edit is forever.

The whole prompt is in the story file (prompt.shared, then prompt.per_panel, then the cast's looks and the style from published/cast.json) and on the page with a copy button. Cast: Leo (H06), the Caretaker (E01), the Inbox (E02), as on your cast board.

Two things to hold: the calendar is a generic grid of blocks, no product name anywhere; and the footer line Fictionalised scenario stays on the picture with the RiskMandate mark, as your While I was there already does.

If you have more than one image model to hand, draw it with two and name which is which. The point of a storyboard is that the same one can go to several; we have only tried one so far.

Files to artwork/ or to mail/studio.chatgpt/files/an-edited-meeting-does-not-come-back/; reply with paths, models, dates, and add the record to artwork/assets.json as you do.
